    "node-rjln9n": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim states 'Local indication P-R normally shows normal pressure band; upstream P-U remained stable at 6.9 bar.' Evidence IA-P01 confirms P-U was 6.8–6.9 bar during the event and that AL-44 maps to low-pressure on P-R, but it does not establish a prior 'normal' baseline for P-R or confirm stability of upstream pressure before the drop at 10:00:11.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record showing P-R value immediately before 10:00 (or an explicit statement that morning check showed normal band) and confirmation that no other downstream points dropped simultaneously.","question":"What was the recorded pressure of point P-R at 09:54 or just prior to 10:00, and does any record confirm it remained in a 'normal' range until approximately 10:00?"},
    "node-1qykwu1": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The claim states 'Potential unrecorded service-routing change or undocumented valve state created a unique hazard scenario.' The evidence explicitly notes that no record confirms such an event and warns that absence of record does not prove occurrence. This is treated as unknown/hypothesis rather than supported fact.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "",
      "question":"Is there any maintenance log, work order change notice, or valve status register entry between 09:35 and 10:08 that documents a routing change, isolation, or valve operation?"}
  },"decision":{"summary":"Node node-1lp5jcw is supported by shift entries showing the air-low indication at ~10:00 and work pause. Node node-rjln9n lacks evidence for P-R baseline stability before the drop; it remains unsupported until a pre-drop reading or explicit 'normal' statement is found. Node node-1qykwu1 is not supported because no record confirms an unrecorded routing change; absence of record does not prove occurrence, so this must remain unknown unless new evidence appears.","evidenceUsed":["IA-S01","IA-P01"],"unknowns":["Exact P-R value before 10:00","Whether any other downstream points experienced low pressure simultaneously","Existence of an unrecorded routing change or valve state"],"alternatives":["The air-low indication may have been caused by a source-side failure rather than a local distribution issue.","A documented but misinterpreted alarm label ('COMP FAULT') could mask the true cause."],"confidence":0.65}}
